check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7642748Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7653750Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7759208Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7769629Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7770358Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7770970Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7771225Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7771434Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7771930Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7772232Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7773164Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7774160Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7774481Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7775076Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7775977Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7776975Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7777552Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7777763Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7777938Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7778213Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7778409Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7778806Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7778937Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7779043Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7779200Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7779522Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7780003Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7784285Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7784490Z I will:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7784798Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7785097Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7785774Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7786496Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7787139Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7787591Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7788020Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7788672Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7789290Z    /root
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7800519Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7801401Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7813107Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7814269Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7814552Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7815534Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:08.7816030Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
