check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2860866Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2868921Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2957536Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2966883Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2967519Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2968327Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2968676Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2969012Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2969671Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2970094Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2970337Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2971350Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2971825Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2972369Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2973416Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2974364Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2974880Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2975202Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2975609Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2975989Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2976227Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2976802Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2977101Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2977330Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2977594Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2978049Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2978938Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2979258Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2979523Z I will:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2979818Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2980043Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2981078Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2981635Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2982320Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2982898Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2983319Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2983982Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2984525Z    /root
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2991493Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.2992757Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3001252Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3002138Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3004343Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3005358Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3006053Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3020235Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3021307Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3029073Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3030064Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3030597Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3030897Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3031243Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3031566Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3031828Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3032447Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3033192Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3033527Z If you would like to
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3033977Z see the output, try like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3034242Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3034548Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3035247Z   $ sh ./install-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3035554Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:14.3039985Z 
